"""Original bathroom planning chapters plus the established HomeCostEngine budget method."""
from pathlib import Path
import runpy,copy
base=runpy.run_path(str(Path(__file__).with_name('renovation-blueprint.py')))
CHAPTERS=[]
def chapter(title,deck,paragraphs,example,rows,conclusion,prompts,checks,task):
    CHAPTERS.append(dict(title=title,deck=deck,paragraphs=paragraphs,example=example,rows=rows,conclusion=conclusion,prompts=prompts,checks=checks,task=task))
def method(index,title):
    c=copy.deepcopy(base['CHAPTERS'][index]);c['title']=title
    for key in ['deck','example','conclusion','task']:c[key]=c[key].replace('renovation','bathroom renovation')
    c['paragraphs']=[p.replace('renovation','bathroom renovation').replace('Make the kitchen usable for two cooks','Make the bathroom usable for the household').replace('buy new cabinets','buy a new vanity') for p in c['paragraphs']]
    CHAPTERS.append(c)

method(0,'Define the bathroom project brief')
chapter('Document the existing bathroom','Make a room record before choosing replacements.',[
'Inventory the fixtures, floor, walls, ceiling, storage, ventilation and lighting. Give each item a retain, replace, relocate or investigate status. A dated record helps everyone see the starting condition and distinguishes a cosmetic update from work that opens or alters the room assembly.',
'Use a simple sketch with photo references for visible conditions. Record room dimensions, doors, windows, fixture locations and access routes. Owner measurements support planning only. The installer or fabricator must verify dimensions and the actual site before ordering products that depend on an exact fit.',
'Record staining, damaged finishes, movement or prior repairs as observations rather than diagnoses. Ask the responsible professional what investigation is needed and what evidence supports the proposed remedy. A repair allowance represents funding for uncertainty; it does not identify a leak source or establish structural suitability.',
'Discuss building age and suspect finishes before disturbance. EPA renovation guidance explains lead-related considerations in older housing [5]. Ask an appropriately qualified contractor about the scope and any other material assessment needed. This record does not authorize demolition, testing or entry into an unsafe area.'
], 'An owner inventories 12 components: five retained, five replaced and two awaiting assessment. The unresolved items stay open instead of being silently priced at zero.', [('Retain','5 items'),('Replace','5 items'),('Investigate','2 items'),('Total recorded components','12 items')],
'The inventory count is a decision aid, not a condition score. Give each investigation an owner and a deadline before dependent purchases.',
['Dated sketch / visible-condition photo references','Retain / replace / relocate inventory','Observed concerns / professional reviewer','Building history / material assessment questions','Open investigations / deadlines / affected orders'],
['Observed symptoms and diagnoses are separated.','Final fit measurements have an assigned verifier.','No unsafe investigation is expected from the owner.'], 'Give the same room record to every contractor invited to provide a final proposal.')

chapter('Choose the layout and access priorities','A moved fixture can change several trades at once.',[
'Start with how the household uses the bathroom: bathing, getting ready, storage and movement through the room. Record privacy needs and any access priorities, including future needs. A functional brief helps a designer evaluate options before a product or a showroom image fixes the layout prematurely.',
'Compare a retained layout with the proposed change on complete scope. Moving a toilet or shower can affect drainage, supply, floor and wall openings, waterproofing, electrical work and restoration. A structural or utility question needs professional review rather than an assumption hidden inside a fixture allowance.',
'Ask the designer and relevant trades to confirm usable clearances, door and screen movement, product dimensions and applicable requirements. This guide gives no universal clearance, accessibility certification or construction specification. Record the approved drawing and the people responsible for verifying its practical use.',
'Rank optional layout upgrades separately from required work. Confirm who approves a revision and which orders depend on it. An apparently small change after waterproofing, cabinetry or glass measurement can create a larger replacement task, so keep the approval sequence visible.'
], 'A fictional retained-layout option is $14,000. A comparable moved-layout option adds $1,400 plumbing, $500 electrical changes and $900 defined restoration. Other potential differences are excluded.', [('Retained-layout option','$14,000'),('Defined relocation additions','$2,800'),('Moved-layout comparison','$16,800'),('Premium for this comparison','$2,800')],
'The premium is invented, not a typical price. Confirm investigation, design, permits and any additional assembly work before either option becomes a complete budget.',
['Household use / privacy / access priorities','Retained and proposed plans / version dates','Utility and structural questions / reviewers','Added scope by trade / restoration / exclusions','Approval record / dependent selections / order dates'],
['Every move has its connected scope identified.','Professionals verify layout and product compatibility.','Access goals are not mistaken for a certified design.'], 'Ask for a scope-matched retained-layout alternative before committing to fixture relocation.')

method(2,'Build the all-in bathroom budget')
method(3,'Write a scope that covers the whole room')

chapter('Investigate moisture before pricing finishes','Address the cause as well as the visible damage.',[
'Record the location, timing and visible signs of a moisture concern without deciding its cause. A stain after a shower, a recurring damaged joint and an unexplained damp floor may require different investigations. Have the appropriate professional assess the condition before a finish-only quote is accepted.',
'EPA moisture guidance emphasizes correcting the water problem as well as dealing with mold [2]. This handbook does not give a cleanup procedure or diagnose a health risk. Ask a suitably qualified provider to define the necessary work and precautions for the actual condition, particularly where damage or contamination is uncertain.',
'Keep investigation, repair and finish restoration as distinct scope lines when that makes responsibility clearer. Record what will be exposed, who assesses it and who approves the remedy. If the contractor excludes concealed damage, agree the evidence, pricing basis and written change process before opening the room.',
'A reserve can fund unresolved work but cannot substitute for a diagnosis. Record which questions remain open after the investigation and what would trigger another decision. Do not spend the entire contingency simply because it appears in the budget; reconcile approved repairs against their actual scope.'
], 'A fictional assessed repair has $250 investigation, $650 defined cause-correction work and $400 finish restoration. These lines are expressly separate and contain no duplicated labor.', [('Investigation','$250'),('Defined repair','$650'),('Finish restoration','$400'),('Known assessed scope','$1,300')],
'This sum demonstrates scope accounting only. It is not an assessment of damage, a remediation protocol or a price estimate for another property.',
['Observed moisture / timing / photo references','Qualified assessor / findings / evidence','Investigation / remedy / restoration scope owners','Known cost / allowance / unresolved conditions','Completion evidence / follow-up / approval record'],
['The cause is professionally assessed.','Repair and cosmetic restoration are distinguished.','A reserve is not treated as an automatic invoice.'], 'Resolve the assessment and responsibility questions before ordering replacement finishes.')

chapter('Plan demolition, protection and temporary access','Removal is more than taking the old fixtures away.',[
'Describe exactly what is removed and what remains. Include fixtures, wall and floor finishes, cabinetry and accessories by location. Identify the protection required for retained items and adjacent rooms. A demolition allowance with no boundaries makes it difficult to compare bids or decide whether a later task is additional work.',
'Assign utility isolation, disconnection, removal, disposal and any required assessment to the responsible qualified providers. This book provides no instructions for disconnecting plumbing or electrical equipment or disturbing suspect materials. Ask who coordinates the sequence and what must be verified before work starts.',
'Plan access for occupants, debris movement, deliveries and any temporary facilities. A one-bath home has different occupancy constraints from a home with another available bathroom. Agree how interruptions are communicated and how the contractor separates the work area from occupied spaces.',
'Record disposal and container fees, protection, cleaning and any finish restoration outside the bathroom. Confirm how an extra layer or unexpected condition is documented and priced. Do not count the same removal or disposal task inside both a fixture replacement package and a separate demolition line.'
], 'A fictional removal scope includes $700 labor, $240 disposal and $160 agreed protection. Utility work is separately included in the relevant trade contract.', [('Removal labor','$700'),('Disposal','$240'),('Defined protection','$160'),('Removal and protection subtotal','$1,100')],
'Utility work is not missing merely because it is excluded here, provided its separate contract clearly includes it. Reconcile the interfaces before approving the whole project.',
['Remove / retain schedule / location references','Disconnection / assessment / qualified trade owners','Occupancy access / protection / interruption contacts','Disposal / container / cleaning / fees','Unexpected-condition evidence / rate / approval process'],
['Removal tasks have defined boundaries.','Retained finishes and occupied areas are addressed.','Disconnect and reconnect responsibilities are assigned.'], 'Review the removal and protection scope with the contractor before confirming the start date.')

chapter('Specify the shower assembly before the tile','The finish selection does not define the water-control system.',[
'Ask the installer to describe the complete proposed shower assembly, including substrate, water-control components, drain interfaces, corners, penetrations and transitions. Record the selected system and the responsible design or installation guidance. A tile quotation alone does not establish the scope of work behind it.',
'Keep product compatibility and installation requirements with the responsible professional. This guide does not supply membrane details, slope specifications or a construction method. Ask which components are included, which are retained and how the selected assembly connects to the actual room condition.',
'Coordinate valves, niches, screens, benches and accessories before the assembly is finalized. An added penetration or revised opening can affect several components. Ask who reviews proposed changes, which evidence is retained before concealment and what checks or approvals apply to this specific work.',
'Write completion evidence and warranty responsibility into the scope discussion. Owner photos are useful records, but do not replace required inspection or the professional judgment needed to accept the assembly. Keep installer documents and product records beside the final bathroom file.'
], 'For fictional scope comparison, $1,800 assembly labor and materials exclude a $220 drain component and $280 agreed preparation task. No other connected scope is assumed included.', [('Defined assembly line','$1,800'),('Excluded drain component','$220'),('Additional preparation','$280'),('Comparison subtotal','$2,300')],
'If the assembly line already contains the drain or preparation, remove the duplicate. This subtotal is not a waterproofing design or a local installed price.',
['Selected assembly / installer / specification source','Substrate / drain / corners / transitions / inclusions','Fixtures and accessories affecting the assembly','Checks / approvals / evidence before concealment','Warranty scope / substitutions / change approvals'],
['The complete assembly is described.','A qualified professional verifies compatibility.','Finish appearance is not mistaken for completion evidence.'], 'Request the written assembly scope before comparing two shower proposals.')

chapter('Coordinate tubs, screens and enclosure glass','Order dimensions after the responsible checks.',[
'Record the selected tub or enclosure model, installation information and intended layout. Identify who verifies support, clearances, plumbing connections and the actual site. A nominal product size is not an authorization to fabricate adjoining components or modify a structure.',
'Ask the relevant supplier when final measurement can take place. Custom screens or glass may depend on completed surfaces and confirmed openings. Keep the measurement owner, drawing version and approval point visible so a late finish change does not quietly invalidate a previously accepted order.',
'Compare complete installed scope: product, accessories, delivery, removal, connection, protection and restoration. Some prices describe only supply or a standard installation assumption. Confirm which site conditions or custom details would change the quote before accepting it.',
'Keep product care instructions and warranty responsibilities together. Ask how installation or damage issues are documented and who returns to resolve them. A polished brochure does not establish which company handles the finished interface between glass, enclosure, tile and waterproofing.'
], 'A fictional screen order is $900 supply plus $250 installation and $80 delivery. Its written quote states that measurement is included. Existing-screen removal is separately included elsewhere.', [('Screen supply','$900'),('Installation','$250'),('Delivery','$80'),('Defined order total','$1,230')],
'Do not add a second measurement charge if it is already included. Confirm custom details, removal, tax and any connected repair responsibilities separately.',
['Exact product / installation information / layout','Support and clearance verification / responsible trades','Final measurement timing / approver / drawing','Supply / delivery / install / removal boundaries','Care / warranty / damage / interface responsibility'],
['Fabrication uses professionally confirmed dimensions.','Measurement timing matches the finished surfaces.','The complete installed scope is understood.'], 'Confirm the measurement and approval sequence before paying for a custom enclosure.')

chapter('Calculate tile purchases and layout allowances','Net area and packaged order quantity are different records.',[
'Measure each finish zone separately on a planning sketch: shower walls, floor, other wall areas and any decorative feature. Label openings, edges and transitions. An owner calculation can check arithmetic, but the installer must confirm the layout and final takeoff before material purchase.',
'Apply a stated ordering allowance only after identifying the net area and intended layout. Product format, pattern, cuts and retained spares can change the appropriate amount. An example percentage is not a universal rule, and waste included in a contractor order should not be added again as an owner expense.',
'Use the actual package coverage and round up to whole cartons after calculating the allowance. Keep material quantities distinct from installation quantities and identify separate trim pieces. Confirm return conditions and spare-stock decisions before assuming the excess order will generate a credit.',
'List setting materials, substrate work, water-control assembly, labor and finish details separately when they are not included in the quoted package. A tile material subtotal does not establish the price of a complete shower or floor. Record who verifies product suitability for the intended use.'
], 'A fictional net tile zone is 90 sq ft. A selected 12% ordering allowance gives 100.8 sq ft. Cartons cover 10 sq ft each, so the order rounds up to 11 cartons at an invented $45 each.', [('Net area','90 sq ft'),('With 12% allowance','100.8 sq ft'),('Whole-carton order','11 cartons'),('Material: 11 × $45','$495')],
'Coverage and allowance are example inputs. Installed labor, trim, preparation, waterproofing, setting materials and tax are not included in the $495.',
['Zone IDs / dimensions / net area / sketch','Selected tile / intended use / installer confirmation','Layout allowance / reason / package coverage','Whole-carton count / trim / retained spares','Material versus installed scope / returns / exclusions'],
['Rounding happens after the allowance is applied.','Package coverage matches the selected tile.','Material cost is not presented as complete installed cost.'], 'Have the installer approve the final quantities and layout before ordering tile.')

chapter('Budget vanity, storage and the countertop','Coordinate the cabinet, basin and connection as a package.',[
'Record the vanity configuration, storage needs, mounting arrangement and intended basin and counter. A furniture-style unit and a built-to-order cabinet may have different supply and installation boundaries. Ask who confirms the complete fit with the room and adjacent fixtures.',
'Identify hardware, panels, tops, cutouts, mirrors and accessories that are included or excluded. Some packaged vanities include a basin but not the faucet or connection work. Keep the original quote beside the selection schedule so a small change does not create a second charge for an already-included component.',
'Coordinate drawer access, door movement, plumbing and electrical interfaces through the responsible installers. Final dimensions and any required supports must be verified before ordering or fabrication. This workbook is an approval record, not a template for cutting a counter or modifying the cabinet.',
'Record delivery, removal, installation, finish restoration and damage reporting. If the owner supplies the vanity, agree who handles missing parts and compatibility questions. Keep warranty and care information with the final fixture record so the household knows whom to contact after completion.'
], 'A fictional vanity package is $850 including cabinet, top and basin. A faucet is $150 and defined installation is $400. Removal is already included in demolition.', [('Cabinet, top and basin','$850'),('Faucet','$150'),('Defined installation','$400'),('Package with installation','$1,400')],
'Do not add basin supply or removal again. Verify what the installation line includes and list any separate plumbing, restoration or tax charges.',
['Cabinet / top / basin / faucet model references','Included hardware and accessories / exclusions','Fit and interfaces / final measurement owner','Delivery / removal / install / restoration boundaries','Owner-supply responsibilities / care / warranty'],
['Package inclusions are checked against selected items.','Fit is confirmed before ordering.','Removal and fixture supply are not duplicated.'], 'Ask for one complete vanity scope showing every included product and trade responsibility.')

chapter('Choose fixtures with the plumbing scope visible','Water efficiency and installation are separate comparisons.',[
'List the toilet, basin fittings, shower controls and other plumbing products by exact model and intended location. Distinguish replacement at the same location from altered piping or drainage. Have the plumbing professional verify compatibility and the complete connection scope before orders become fixed.',
'Record removal, disposal, installation, shutoffs, access and finish restoration where applicable. An appealing fixture price does not establish what happens behind the wall. If a condition is unresolved, identify the investigation and approval process rather than treating it as included at no charge.',
'EPA WaterSense information explains the role of its label in water-efficiency and performance comparisons [3]. Verify the actual selected model and its suitability with the installer. Household water use depends on behavior and site conditions; a general product claim is not a promised saving for this project.',
'Coordinate rough-in requirements, controls and trim with the approved assembly before concealment. Keep product specifications, approved substitutions and completion checks together. This book gives no plumbing installation instructions, pressure specification or diagnosis of existing pipe condition.'
], 'Two fictional showerheads have listed flows of 2.5 and 2.0 gallons per minute. At an assumed eight-minute use, the arithmetic difference is four gallons. No annual usage or bill saving is assumed.', [('Model A: 2.5 × 8','20 gallons'),('Model B: 2.0 × 8','16 gallons'),('Difference for assumed use','4 gallons'),('Actual household saving','Not established')],
'Use verified model data and realistic use assumptions. The calculation is a comparison method, not proof that either product suits the existing plumbing.',
['Exact fixture models / locations / specification sheets','Professional compatibility and condition assessment','Remove / connect / access / restore scope','Verified model performance / usage assumptions','Substitutions / completion checks / warranty record'],
['Plumbing suitability has a qualified reviewer.','Rough-in and finish selections are coordinated.','Illustrative use is not advertised as guaranteed savings.'], 'Finalize the fixture schedule with the plumber and assembly installer before concealed work closes.')

chapter('Define electrical, lighting and heated features','Price complete endpoints with professional verification.',[
'List the planned lights, outlets, fan controls and optional heated features on the layout. Record the function of each endpoint and whether a fitting is replaced or the installation changes. A product count cannot establish circuit suitability or the scope of work behind the finished surface.',
'Have the electrical professional assess the existing condition, proposed equipment and applicable requirements. Ask which approvals or investigations must be completed before dependent purchases. This handbook does not design wiring, size circuits or prescribe protective devices for bathroom installations.',
'Coordinate fixture models, controls, mirrors and cabinets before finalizing locations. Confirm who supplies each product and whether the quoted installed price already contains it. Heated features should be evaluated on their complete system and installation scope, with compatibility and testing left to the responsible professional.',
'Assign opening, patching and finish restoration responsibility. Record interruption dates and how completion evidence is retained. Keep scope changes tied to endpoint IDs and drawing versions so a late product upgrade can be priced for its full installed effect.'
], 'A fictional quote contains four defined lighting endpoints at $175 each plus $260 fixture supply. The endpoint rate expressly excludes fixture supply. Painting is included in a separate finish contract.', [('Endpoints: 4 × $175','$700'),('Fixtures','$260'),('Defined electrical subtotal','$960'),('Separate finish contract','Already includes painting')],
'The invented rate is not an installation specification. Check the quote boundaries before adding fixtures or restoration to an already complete installed line.',
['Endpoint IDs / locations / functions / layout','Professional assessment / approvals / open questions','Products and controls / compatibility / supply owner','Installed inclusions / access / patching / painting','Interruption dates / completion evidence / changes'],
['Requirements are verified by the qualified trade.','Product supply and installation are counted once.','Restoration has an accountable owner.'], 'Ask the electrician to annotate the approved endpoint list with inclusions and unresolved questions.')

chapter('Plan ventilation as a complete system','A fan price does not confirm an effective installation.',[
'Record the existing ventilation arrangement and any observed humidity or odor concern. Ask the responsible professional to assess the room, selected equipment and proposed installation. A fan model alone does not establish the actual installed airflow or a suitable solution for an unresolved moisture problem.',
'Include the equipment, route, termination where applicable, controls, electrical connection and restoration in the scope discussion. Assign interfaces with ceilings, walls or roof work to named trades. This guide provides no airflow formula, duct design or instruction for cutting an opening.',
'ENERGY STAR ventilation-fan guidance describes efficiency and noise-related considerations for comparing equipment [4]. Use selected model information alongside professional system review. An efficient product label does not establish that the proposed installation is suitable for this bathroom.',
'Agree how completion will be checked and what operating and maintenance information the owner receives. Record any substitution before installation so the responsible professional can confirm it. Keep the fan and control manuals in the bathroom project record rather than relying on a generic sales description.'
], 'A fictional complete fan scope separates $220 equipment, $330 route work, $150 connection and $100 restoration. Each line has been confirmed as non-overlapping.', [('Equipment','$220'),('Route and connection','$480'),('Restoration','$100'),('Defined scope subtotal','$800')],
'The subtotal illustrates scope accounting only. Confirm any excluded assessment, permit or installation requirement before treating the proposal as complete.',
['Existing arrangement / observed issue / assessor','Selected fan and control / model documents','Route / termination / connection / restoration owners','Professional verification / exclusions / approvals','Completion checks / operating guidance / maintenance'],
['Product efficiency is distinct from installed suitability.','Every interface has a responsible trade.','An unresolved moisture cause remains visible.'], 'Request the complete installed ventilation scope, not only the fan model and purchase price.')

chapter('Schedule finishes and life during the remodel','A usable bathroom and a finished project are different milestones.',[
'Identify the painting, trim, accessory and final-cleaning scope left after the major installation tasks. Give each mirror, rail, holder and other fitting a location and supply responsibility. Coordinate attachment requirements with the responsible installer before finished surfaces are altered.',
'Plan the periods when the bathroom will be unavailable and how the household will manage them. Ask the responsible trades to confirm installation, checking and readiness-to-use timing for the selected systems. Do not infer that a surface is ready for normal use just because the room looks finished.',
'Budget additional storage, temporary facilities or accommodation only where they are part of the actual household plan. Separate additional project spending from ordinary living costs. A temporary arrangement should have a start date, expected duration and decision trigger if the schedule changes.',
'Keep a punch list with responsible people and dates. Coordinate final cleaning and protection around any outstanding work so one trade does not damage another completed surface. Close out the room with product records, approval evidence and clear service contacts, not only a final invoice.'
], 'A fictional household budgets $45 per day for an additional temporary arrangement over 10 days, plus $120 storage. Ordinary household expenses are excluded.', [('Temporary arrangement: 10 × $45','$450'),('Storage','$120'),('Known additional living cost','$570'),('Three extra days at $45','$135 more')],
'The daily cost is invented. Use actual arrangements and dates; the example does not authorize delay charges or establish when an assembly is ready to use.',
['Remaining finishes / accessories / location schedule','Unavailable periods / readiness confirmation / trades','Temporary arrangement / dates / additional costs','Delay trigger / contacts / budget decision','Punch list / cleaning / protection / service records'],
['Use timing is confirmed by responsible professionals.','Ordinary living expenses are not double-counted.','Outstanding tasks have an owner and completion date.'], 'Agree the temporary-bathroom and finish plan before demolition is booked.')

